comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T17:57:51.200Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status search for transcript successful exit, no_effect, and partial_effect found canonical exit-contract owner pm-hqa8g1 and the active transcript owner pm-8pnj, but no item for this PR #1133 parser contradiction; creating one review-caught child issue rather than duplicating either owner."
  "2026-08-27T18:17:28.812Z","harness:codex","Review resolution evidence for PR #1133: reused isPmSuccessfulExitCode plus the command-specific exit declaration; non-refusal transcripts accept exit 6/7 only for commands that declare them, refusals reject all successful exits, and the real corpus now executes close-many partial_effect=7 and no_effect=6 from stdout. Focused linked tests passed; full coverage passed 8,063 tests at exact 100/100/100/100; pnpm quality:static passed."
  "2026-08-27T22:34:58.312Z","harness:codex","Lifecycle reconciliation: the historical docs_add event is immutable and remains visible after its original close/release. Ownership is now explicitly reacquired before this corrective evidence entry; future closeout metadata must precede close and release."
  "2026-08-28T03:22:47.799Z","harness:codex","Review wording correction: the changelog is generated from PM titles. Updated this canonical title to state the implemented behavior: non-refusal transcript steps accept no_effect and partial_effect only when the invoked command declares those successful exits. Refusal steps and undeclared effect exits remain rejected."
  "2026-08-28T03:44:19.934Z","harness:codex","TDD red evidence: node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/sdk/output-contracts.spec.ts failed exactly at the bulk-effects transcript after adding --json before close-many and value-consuming --pm-path before update-many. The parser resolved args[0] as the command and rejected declared exit 6 before reaching the second case."
  "2026-08-28T03:57:21.590Z","harness:codex","Exact-head Greptile resolution evidence: the parser now reuses parseBootstrapCommandName instead of args[0], covers --json before close-many and --pm-path <value> before update-many, and rejects a flag-only invocation with no command. Focused output/transcript tests passed 28/28, bootstrap tests passed 99/99, the linked PM test passed, full coverage passed 585 files and 8,076 tests at statements 59,941/59,941, branches 45,130/45,130, functions 12,466/12,466, lines 57,722/57,722, and CI=1 pnpm quality:static passed."
  "2026-08-28T04:27:57.471Z","harness:codex","Active review recurrence: exact-head Greptile correctly found that parser validation now resolves global prefixes canonically but the executable token-gate replay still calls resolvePmCommandOutputEnvelope(step.args[0]). Reusing this canonical item because it already owns the gate, parser, bulk-effect replay, and global-prefix recurrence; no new item is warranted."
  "2026-08-28T04:28:55.097Z","harness:codex","TDD red evidence for the replay-layer recurrence: changing the direct validation step to args [--json, list] made the focused agent-task token-gate suite fail exactly with output contract drift diagnostic != collection at validateSuccessfulOutput, while the other eight tests passed."
  "2026-08-28T04:48:12.908Z","harness:codex","Exact-head replay-layer correction evidence: validateSuccessfulOutput now resolves the invoked command with parseBootstrapCommandName before consulting the output-envelope contract, and fails closed when global flags contain no command. The focused parser/bootstrap/gate suite passed 127/127, the real five-task fourteen-step replay passed at 4,349 composite estimated tokens, full coverage passed 585 files and 8,081 tests at statements 59,951/59,951, branches 45,137/45,137, functions 12,467/12,467, and lines 57,732/57,732, and CI-mode static quality passed."
  "2026-08-28T05:09:45.084Z","harness:codex","Review architecture recurrence: CodeRabbit found task-transcript-contracts imports cli-bootstrap, pulling runtime/bootstrap dependencies into the contract-only SDK entrypoint. The correction will extract the canonical command scanner into a contract-only module while preserving existing CLI and SDK exports."
  "2026-08-28T05:10:41.068Z","harness:codex","TDD red: the contract-boundary regression found src/sdk/agent/task-transcript-contracts.ts still importing ../cli-bootstrap.js and could not find the intended contract-only scanner dependency."
  "2026-08-28T05:36:51.224Z","harness:codex","Correction evidence: source-boundary regression coverage rejects any task-transcript import of cli-bootstrap and requires the contract-only scanner; focused SDK/bootstrap/recovery suites pass; SDK surface reports zero classified changes; entrypoint-cost, build, full coverage, and all static quality gates pass. Fresh-directory transcript acceptance resolved a command after a leading global flag."
  "2026-08-28T06:38:33.997Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review reconciliation: actual_result now states both primary acceptance outcomes—command-declared effect-aware successful exits 0, 6, and 7 are accepted, and command identity is resolved after global prefixes by the shared contract-only scanner."
learnings[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-27T18:17:29.321Z","harness:codex","A transport status is not synonymous with failure: parsing, stream selection, and transcript validation must share the canonical effect-aware exit contract so exits 6 and 7 remain successful without becoming globally legal for every command."
  "2026-08-28T03:57:22.139Z","harness:codex","Transcript contracts must derive command identity with the same bootstrap grammar as runtime dispatch; positional args[0] assumptions drift as soon as global flags are legal before a command."
  "2026-08-28T04:48:13.436Z","harness:codex","Command identity must be resolved once through the canonical bootstrap grammar at every contract-consumption layer; fixing only the public parser leaves executable replay and assurance code vulnerable to the same positional args[0] recurrence."
  "2026-08-28T05:36:50.722Z","harness:codex","A contract-only public entrypoint must not reach through a runtime aggregator for a small parser primitive. Extract pure dependency-light primitives, then preserve existing public wrapper signatures at compatibility entrypoints."
